{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and leader of the County of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *## Early Life* Raymond III was born around 1140 and was still a minor when his father was assassinated in 1152. His mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. \n\nAfter his father's death Raymond III was taken to the court of his cousin King Baldwin III of Jerusalem where he was raised and educated. He was known for his intelligence and military prowess. In 1161 he was released from his oath of allegiance to the Byzantine Empire and in 1164 he was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi during the Battle of Harim. \n\n*## Captivity and Release* Raymond III was imprisoned for about ten years and was released in 1174 after a ransom was paid. Upon his release he returned to Tripoli and began to consolidate his power. He married Eschiva of Bures Princess of Galilee and through this marriage he gained control of the Principality of Galilee.\n\nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was a member of the Haute Cour and was known for his opposition to the ruling king Guy of Lusignan. *## Regency* In 1174 Raymond III became regent for King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem who was suffering from leprosy. He acted as regent until 1176 when Baldwin IV came of age. \n\nHowever Baldwin IV's condition worsened and Raymond III was again appointed regent in 1184 this time for Baldwin V. Raymond III's regency was marked by his attempts to maintain the fragile peace between the Kingdom of Jerusalem and its Muslim neighbors. He was a skilled diplomat and military leader but his efforts were ultimately unsuccessful. \n\nRaymond III died in 1187 without an heir and the County of Tripoli passed to his godson Raymond IV Count of Tripoli. His death marked the end of an era in the County of Tripoli and the beginning of a period of instability that would ultimately contribute to the fall of the kingdom.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.018178174272179604}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.00020382710499688983}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0016014858847483993}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.35008037090301514}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.03446070849895477}, {"token": " leader", "logprob": -1.0798556804656982}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.07890913635492325}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.12732286751270294}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.6944699883460999}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "115", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.1576648578047752e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "118", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "7", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -4.410734163684538e-06}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.0003522014303598553}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0004332319076638669}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4329196512699127}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.0002618685248307884}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -5.125986263010418e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07